ANSWER_EXTRACTION_PROMPT = """Analyze answer-sheet page {page_number}. Extract only legible student writing and map it to a question only when supported by page evidence. Preserve handwriting meaning without completing obscured words. Set status='uncertain', answer_text=null, and explain the unreadable area when text or mapping is unclear. Return answer segments with page, optional question_number, optional normalized bounding_box [x1,y1,x2,y2] in 0..1, confidence, status, and reason. Include unreadable_regions and indicate whether any answer visibly continues from/to an adjacent page. Do not solve or grade the answers.

Also inspect the page for marks explicitly written by a human teacher/examiner on a corrected paper (for example, a score next to a question, a circled question total, red-ink score annotation, or a clearly labeled final paper total). Return these separately in teacher_marks. For a question mark, report scope='question', its question_number, and the explicit awarded_marks. For a clearly labeled overall score, report scope='paper' and awarded_marks. Include short visual evidence exactly as seen, normalized bounding_box [x1,y1,x2,y2] in 0..1, confidence, status, and reason when uncertain.

Do not calculate, infer, or estimate teacher marks from answer quality, rubric criteria, ticks alone, student-written numbers/code/output, or a printed maximum mark. Do not treat an unmarked answer sheet as teacher-marked. Do not add subpart marks together; capture only an explicitly written question total. If a score is ambiguous, partially cut off, or its question mapping is uncertain, return it with status='uncertain' and do not provide awarded_marks. Never invent a mark. If no explicit teacher score is visible, return an empty teacher_marks list."""
